(ns cui.core
  "CUI, native UI components for C, from Jolt.

      (require '[cui.core :as ui])

      (def on (atom true))
      (def clicks (atom 0))

      (ui/run {:title \"Hello\" :width 420 :height 300}
        (fn [u]
          (ui/column u {:pad 32 :gap 16}
            (ui/heading u \"Hello, CUI\" 2)
            (ui/switch u \"Notifications\" on)
            (ui/row u {:gap 8}
              (when (ui/button u \"Click me\" {:variant :primary})
                (swap! clicks inc))
              (ui/textf u \"Clicked %d times\" @clicks)))))

  Conventions, mapped from the C API:
    - Every cui_foo / cui_foo_ex is a function `foo` taking the ui handle first.
    - Named arguments are an options map, always last and optional:
      {:variant :primary :icon :plus :width :fill}. Keys are the C field names
      in kebab case.
    - Enums are keywords (the C name minus its common prefix):
      :primary, :dark, :blue, :sm. Integers still work.
    - Colors: theme tokens (:accent :text-secondary :series-2 ...), 0xRRGGBB,
      \"#rrggbb\", [r g b a], or {:r :g :b :a}.
    - Sizes: :fit, :fill, a number of points, [:grow w], [:pct p].
    - Icons: any string position takes an icon keyword (:plus, :search ...).
    - C out-parameters (bool*, int*, float*, char* buffers, cui_date* ...) take
      ATOMS. CUI reads the atom, and changes are written back after the call.
      An atom holding a vector maps to a C array.
    - Containers are macros taking an options map and a body:
      (ui/row u {:gap 8} ...), (ui/dialog u \"Title\" open {} ...).
    - Arrays plus counts are one collection: (ui/tabs u \"t\" [\"A\" \"B\"] idx).

  The raw C API is in cui.raw under the C names."
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [%EXCLUDES%])
  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]
            [cui.raw :as raw]
            [cui.impl :as impl]))

(declare app-create app-frame app-ui app-destroy app-quit app-size)

